WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:11.400
Cambridge, you have to remember, had all kinds
of factories when I was a kid growing up.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.240
We had Lever Brothers, we still have a little
bit of Necco, but you had all kinds of little

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:26.090
shops. And probably one of the most notable
one, they had a donut shop on Main Street.

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:37.989
And you could always smell the donuts. They
still have Paul's, which is a corner store,

00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:47.170
and even though we grew up and left, people
still come back to Paul's just for a sub.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:55.479
Primarily a meatball sub, because no one makes
a better meatball sub than Paul's Variety

00:00:55.479 --> 00:01:09.789
down on School Street. Cambridge was just
so wonderful, so memorable growing up. If

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:15.560
there was ever an all-American city it would
have to have been Cambridge. Of course you

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:23.130
would've had to have been here to know that,
to experience it, and to appreciate it. I

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:27.869
went to Roberts School which is called the
Maynard now, it's on the corner of Windsor

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:36.530
and Harvard Street. I lived in that community
all my life. When you're a young man, a little

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:40.899
kid, it's a big school. All my friends went
there. When we went to school, you'd go in

00:01:40.899 --> 00:01:47.659
the morning and come home at lunch, then go
back in the afternoon. Everybody in the community

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:53.270
that I lived in went there. I've got to tell
you, we lived in more of a multicultural community.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:58.850
There were the [family name]s who were Greek,
there were the [family name]s who were Greek.

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:05.009
There was Roseanne and they were Italian,
and there were Portuguese, people from Barbados,

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:10.899
the Harris's, Steven Harris and his family,
Humphrey Harris. And we wandered between the

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:17.360
two projects [name of housing development]
and Newtowne Court. Down there at the gardens,

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.030
down by St. Mary's, and we wanders to St.
Mary's, where we grew up with Timmy Boylan,

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:25.970
a lot of the Irish kids that went to the Catholic
school, the Cape Verdean kids. We were a multicultural

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:35.220
community. It was a community where the statement
today is "It takes a village to raise a family."

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.230
We were that village.

